      narrative: `Superintelligence arrives around 2031 in the Discontinuous branch, and the quantum field spends the decade discovering which of its problems were intellectual and which were physical. The intellectual ones dissolve within two or three years: near-optimal codes and decoders for every modality, control stacks operating at the limits set by measurement, cryogenic CMOS multiplexing that cuts wiring per qubit by orders of magnitude, fabrication recipes approaching the materials floor on two-qubit error (of order 10 to the minus 4 to 10 to the minus 5), and compiled algorithms with gate counts near their lower bounds. The physical ones persist. Wafers take months, fabs take years, cryostats and helium supply take years, and every new process must be characterized on real hardware, so machines lag designs by three to five years. Neutral-atom and photonic architectures, which scale through optics and foundry processes rather than through superconducting wafer yield, advance fastest. Hundreds of logical qubits run by about 2033, thousands by 2035, and a cryptographically relevant machine, whose requirements ASI reduces well below Gidney's 2025 estimate, is plausible in one or two state programs by 2035 to 2037. Every remaining RSA and elliptic-curve deployment is treated as compromised, harvested traffic from the 2010s and 2020s is decrypted, and cryptography moves fully to lattice and hash-based schemes, with ASI-driven cryptanalysis of those schemes an open worry that forces cryptographic agility. Applications are narrower than the 2020s expected: ASI-derived classical methods handle much of chemistry and all of optimization, so quantum machines are reserved for quantum dynamics, strongly correlated matter, nuclear and field-theory simulation, and cryptanalysis. Sensing reaches the Heisenberg limit in deployed instruments, and entangled clock networks span continents. The known-algorithm limitation binds even ASI: the class of problems with exponential quantum speedup grows, but not into NP-hard optimization. The index reaches about 24.`,
